  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5515",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to NCI-H1623, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The evidence indicates that Mollicellin N acts as a target for A704, which in turn is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and both of these are linked to NCI-H1623. Additionally, Mollicellin N is also linked to Leukocyte common antigen, which is targeted by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which also targets NCI-H1623. These pathways suggest that Mollicellin N may influence NCI-H1623 through different molecular mechanisms, potentially through distinct biological processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility that Mollicellin N exerts its effects on NCI-H1623 via multiple routes, possibly through different cellular targets or signaling pathways. The evidence supports a role for Mollicellin N in modulating the activity of downstream molecules that ultimately interact with NCI-H1623, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
